{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ATSWYk1wHGQNM5tTJBupMy","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_12/projects/simgate-modular-routing/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# simgate-modular-routing — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-13 15:37 UTC | 更新原因: Reviewer W1-W5 修订: GPU 单位改 RTX 5090, 2-way 优先, 信号预筛, 参数控制 ablation\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\nSimGate: 显式轻量 router (Qwen3-1.7B) 学习 per-step 安全路由 — 检测 LLM 推理高风险状态，选择性调用确定性外部计算（环境模拟器）防止灾难性失败。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 投稿目标\\\\nEMNLP 2026 ARR short paper (4 pages)，DDL: 2026-05-25（剩余 12 天）\\\\n\\\\n## 当前阶段\\\\n**Research Phase** — MVP PASS (D005)，Dream 模拟中\\\\n\\\\n## 当前进展\\\\n- MVP: DONE (PASS) — 4/5 task types det > internal 显著, 主信号 = death avoidance\\\\n- paper_framing.md: DONE — 2 Claims, safety-aware routing. C1 含待确认子项（selective > unconditional）\\\\n- experiment_plan.yaml: v2 (Reviewer W1-W5 修订) — 2-way 优先, 信号预筛, 参数控制 ablation\\\\n- Dream: RUNNING (dream_20260513T153257, full mode, ~15 min)\\\\n- melt/change-state: Reviewer 确认非重复，但共享 variations → 论文中合并为 \\\\\\\"state-change tasks\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [ ] Dream 完成 → 审阅审稿报告，确认/调整 framing\\\\n- [ ] Dream 通过后批准 plan-001a (信号预筛) + plan-007 (boil rerun) 双卡并行\\\\n- [ ] Agent 完成 gpu1-v3 registry 更新 (ANALYZING → DONE)\\\\n- [ ] plan-001a 完成 → 筛出 10-15 有信号 task types → 启动 plan-001b\\\\n- [ ] plan-001b 完成 → 启动 plan-002 (router SFT) + plan-004 (explicit vs implicit ablation)\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- 服务器: westb-13313, 2× RTX 5090 32GB (cuda:0, cuda:1)\\\\n- P0: ~72h | P1: ~25h | P2: ~25h | 总计: ~122h (RTX 5090 wall-clock hours)\\\\n- Critical path: 001a(10h) → 001b(25h) → 002(8h) → 003(15h) = ~2.5 天双卡并行\\\\n\\\\n## 时间线 (12 天, RTX 5090 双卡)\\\\n| 天数 | 任务 | GPU |\\\\n|------|------|-----|\\\\n| 1 | Dream 审阅 + plan-001a 信号预筛 + plan-007 boil rerun | 双卡 |\\\\n| 2-3 | plan-001b 全量 trajectory collection | 双卡满载 |\\\\n| 4 | plan-002 router SFT + plan-004 explicit/implicit ablation | 双卡 |\\\\n| 5-6 | plan-003 evaluation + plan-006 2/3-way ablation | 双卡 |\\\\n| 7 | plan-005 routing analysis + plan-008 router size (P1) | 单卡+分析 |\\\\n| 8-10 | Paper writing (Paper Agent) | 按需补实验 |\\\\n| 11-12 | Review + submit | — |\\\\n\\\\n## 关键风险\\\\n1. Novelty 天花板 — SFT small router 技术简单，需靠 empirical finding + analysis\\\\n2. C1 子项待确认 — trained router > always-det 尚无证据 (plan-003 验证)\\\\n3. ScienceWorld 单 benchmark — short paper 可接受\\\\n4. Death avoidance 唯一信号 — 全量 collection 可能发现正向引导信号\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-13 | Research phase plan revised per Reviewer W1-W5: 2- | — |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-13 | MVP Phase 1 判定 PASS — det > internal 在 ≥2/5 task t | mvp-p1-gpu0, mvp-p1-gpu0-vllm, mvp-p1-gpu1-v3 |\\\\n| D004 | 2026-05-13 | MVP 判定 primary metric 改为 always-deterministic vs a | — |\\\\n| D003 | 2026-05-13 | GPU0 继续收集 baseline，GPU1 停下修复 tie-break + 致死动作过滤后重跑 | mvp-p1-gpu0, mvp-p1-gpu1-vllm |\\\\n| D002 | 2026-05-13 | 采纳 Reviewer 全部 4 条 warning，修订 MVP 为 Phase 0 + Phas | — |\\\\n| D001 | 2026-05-13 | MVP 方案: ScienceWorld 信号检测——验证确定性模拟是否在规则驱动任务上优于 LLM | — |\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2649, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdgGcBwmrjWomsyFCSi2hd","session_id":"cf927c35-53a0-4107-b5fc-888888fb1cc5","uuid":"15010dda-65db-4bfe-ae56-34b3cf09de30","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:17:45.638Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KDytT1YTxHoLqk2opfBXWF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TdApygYCbx1QpPpn5bLL26","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus: **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"When Does Deterministic Computation Help LLM Agents? A Diagnostic Study on ScienceWorld\"\n\n**Core idea**: Introduces counterfactual evaluation methodology that forks agent trajectories at each decision step across three computation modalities (fast internal, deep CoT, deterministic simulation). Applied to 15 ScienceWorld task types (300 episodes, 6,600 steps). Main findings are negative: learned per-step routing ≈ always-simulate; explicit ≈ implicit routing; routing patterns don't transfer. Positive finding: deterministic computation helps only on 4/15 death-risk task types involving physical state transitions.\n\n**Claimed contributions**:\n1. A counterfactual evaluation methodology (fork trajectories → hindsight scoring → label optimal modality per step)\n2. Per-task diagnostic analysis showing simulation value is sharply task-dependent (4/15 tasks)\n\n**Related work discussed in paper** (8 references):\n- [1] ReAct (Yao et al., ICLR 2023) — reasoning + acting\n- [2] Reflexion (Shinn et al., NeurIPS 2023) — verbal reinforcement learning\n- [3] ScienceWorld (Wang et al., EMNLP 2022) — benchmark\n- [4] CogRouter (Qiao et al., 2024) — RL-based routing, 84.6 on ScienceWorld\n- [5] ITP-R (Lu et al., 2024) — routes to LLM world model, 62.58\n- [6] ReTool (Feng et al., 2024) — RL for tool use\n- [7] ToRA (Gou et al., ICLR 2024) — tool-integrated reasoning\n- [8] DAgger (Ross et al., AISTATS 2011) — imitation learning\n\nNote: References [4] and [5] have placeholder arXiv IDs (arXiv:2405.XXXXX).\n\n**Key results**:\n- SimGate (65.2) vs always-det (64.8): Δ=0.4, not significant\n- Explicit vs implicit routing: Δ=1.2, p=0.38, not significant\n- CogRouter† (84.6) cited but uses different backbone/training — 19.4 point gap\n- Only single environment (ScienceWorld), single backbone (Qwen2.5-7B)\n\n**Paper structure**: 6 pages. Abstract, Introduction, Method (SimGate framework, counterfactual methodology, router training), Experiments (label analysis, main results, per-task diagnostics, explicit vs implicit, ablations, router training analysis), Discussion, Conclusion.\n\n**Framing**: The paper was pivoted from \"safety-aware modular routing\" (original method paper) to \"When Does Deterministic Computation Help?\" (diagnostic/negative-result paper). The pivot was driven by weak results: the proposed routing method provides no advantage over always-simulate.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProvide a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (novelty + related work focus)\n3. **Weaknesses** (novelty + related work focus)\n4. **Questions to authors**\n5. **Novelty assessment**: Is the counterfactual methodology genuinely novel? Is the negative-result framing a sufficient contribution? How does this compare to existing work on tool-use routing, computation allocation, and negative-result studies?\n6. **Related work gaps**: What important related work is missing? Consider: adaptive computation (early exit, mixture of experts), tool-use learning (Toolformer, ART), world models for agents (DreamerV3, IRIS), safe RL / constrained agents, other routing/gating mechanisms.\n7. **Significance rating** (1-5)\n8. **Overall score** (1-6 scale)\n9. **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Evaluate: Does this paper advance the field? Is the negative result informative or expected? Is the framing honest about the limitations? Are the contributions sufficient for a top venue?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25755,"cache_read_input_tokens":22948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25755},"output_tokens":15,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf927c35-53a0-4107-b5fc-888888fb1cc5","uuid":"bb294143-7ef2-43e4-a315-0dedf0c2a7cf"}
